    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** enter May 31 with a clear offensive engine, led by **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56). Both players benefit from high-leverage matchups against vulnerable arms in Littell and Canning, respectively; **Jackson Merrill**\u2019s score remains robust despite the slight penalty for facing an elite defensive catcher, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on a dynamic platoon advantage and a favorable spot in the two-hole. **Kyle Tucker** (74.37) rounds out our top-tier tier, utilizing a wind-aided environment against Painter to maintain elite efficiency. While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a tough test against a 2.95 xERA arm in Miles, his immense raw talent and the significant park factor lift his projection to a comfortable 71.73, ensuring he remains a must-start despite the SP matchup.\n\nOur utilization of the bottom half of the lineup involves a calculated gamble on **Sam Antonacci** (61.66), who draws a favorable matchup against Montero. His xwOBA and lead-off spot outweigh the neutral park factors, nudging him ahead of **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.95), whose score is suppressed by a high-skill matchup against Bradish. The closest decision in the final lineup involved the utility spot; while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** sits on the razor's edge of the \"Strong\" start threshold, he retains the nod over **Brayan Rocchio** (43.08), who is hampered by an unfavorable #9 order slot and a difficult look against Suarez. \n\nWe continue to monitor the heavy injury toll on our roster, as **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Drake Baldwin** remain sidelined, severely limiting our flexibility for late-game defensive substitutions or pinch-hitting opportunities. With the remaining depth options like **Jorge Polanco**, **Josh Lowe**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Heliot Ramos**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Miguel Andujar**, **Coby Mayo**, and **Dominic Smith** currently not providing the requisite efficiency for this specific slate, we are relying on our core starters to maintain the high floor necessary to compete in the 5x5 categories. Pay close attention to **Liam Hicks**; his sub-50 score reflects the volatility of his current matchup, and he represents our most significant risk for failing to provide meaningful value in today\u2019s effort.",
